# Architecture Audit: Dynamic Forms, Data Flow & Multi-Tenancy

## 1. ✅ Dynamic Form Population from Programs Tab

**Yes, the "Reserve a Court" form is fully dynamic.** Here's the exact flow:

```mermaid
graph LR
    A["Programs Tab<br/>(programs.js)"] -->|"Saves to Firestore"| B["academies/{academyId}<br/>(tenantSettings)"]
    B -->|"loadTenantSettings()"| C["shared.js<br/>(in-memory tenantSettings)"]
    C -->|"getBookingHierarchy()"| D["Booking Type → Category → Period<br/>dropdown hierarchy"]
    D -->|"populateBookingDropdowns()"| E["Reserve a Court Form<br/>(dashboard.html)"]
```

### How each program type maps to the form:

| Programs Tab Section | tenantSettings key | Reserve a Court → Booking Type | Category Dropdown |
|---|---|---|---|
| Membership Programs (Individual) | `membership_programs` (type=Individual) | **Members** | Individual |
| Membership Programs (Group) | `membership_programs` (type=Group) | **Group/Lease** | Group Members |
| Spot Booking & Hourly Slots | `hourly_slots` | **Spot booking** / **Guest Play** | Hourly Slot / Peak/Non-Peak |
| Coaching Schedule (Kids/Women/Adults) | `coaching_schedule` | **Coaching** | Kids / Women / Adults |
| Coaching Schedule (Advance Batch) | `coaching_schedule` (category includes "advance") | **Advance Training** | 3 Session |
| Fee Structure (Personal Training) | `fee_structure` (name includes "personal training") | **Personal training** | Private Coaching |

### Code Evidence:
- [getBookingHierarchy()](file:///c:/Users/Admin/Documents/POC/Badminton/js/shared.js#L110-L174) — reads from `tenantSettings` and builds the hierarchy
- [populateBookingDropdowns()](file:///c:/Users/Admin/Documents/POC/Badminton/js/shared.js#L176-L189) — populates the Type dropdown from hierarchy
- [populateCategoryDropdown()](file:///c:/Users/Admin/Documents/POC/Badminton/js/shared.js#L248-L261) — cascading Category dropdown
- [populatePeriodDropdown()](file:///c:/Users/Admin/Documents/POC/Badminton/js/shared.js#L263) — cascading Period dropdown

**When a tenant modifies their programs**, they click "Save All" on the Programs page → it writes to `academies/{academyId}` in Firestore → next time they open the Dashboard, `loadTenantSettings()` fetches the updated data → `getBookingHierarchy()` rebuilds the dropdown options → the Reserve a Court form reflects the changes.

