## 2. ✅ Reserve a Court → Members UI Page Data Flow

**Yes, data flows from Reserve a Court to the Members page.** Here's the flow:

```mermaid
graph TD
    A["Reserve a Court Form<br/>(handleBookingSubmit)"] --> B{"Booking Type?"}
    B -->|"Spot booking / Guest Play"| C["Creates booking only<br/>(no member record)"]
    B -->|"Members / Group/Lease /<br/>Coaching / Advance Training"| D["Creates booking docs<br/>for each day of month"]
    D --> E["Auto-creates member doc<br/>in 'members' collection"]
    B -->|"Personal training"| F["Creates single booking<br/>+ member doc"]
    E --> G["Members UI Page<br/>(members.js)"]
    F --> G
    G --> H["getPlanDetails(planKey)<br/>resolves name + fee"]
```

### What gets stored in the `members` collection:

| Field | Value | Source |
|---|---|---|
| `name` | Customer name | Form input |
| `type` | Plan key (e.g. `Individual_5Days`) | `resolvePlanKey()` matches against `tenantSettings` |
| `joinDate` | Today's date | Auto-generated |
| `lastPaidDate` | Today's date | Auto-generated |
| `bookingId` | First booking document ID | From the batch write |
| `status` | "active" | Default |
| `academyId` | Current user's academy ID | From `currentUser.academyId` |

### Members Page reads this data:
- [loadMembers()](file:///c:/Users/Admin/Documents/POC/Badminton/js/shared.js#L369-L381) — queries `members` collection filtered by `academyId`
- [getPlanDetails()](file:///c:/Users/Admin/Documents/POC/Badminton/js/members.js#L111-L144) — resolves `planKey` back to a human-readable name + monthly fee by looking up against `tenantSettings`
- [renderMembersTable()](file:///c:/Users/Admin/Documents/POC/Badminton/js/members.js#L87-L109) — displays member data with plan name, fee due status, and payment tracking

### Code Evidence:
- [Auto-enrollment for recurring plans](file:///c:/Users/Admin/Documents/POC/Badminton/js/dashboard.js#L601-L615) — `addDoc(collection(db, "members"), {...})`
- [Auto-enrollment for Personal Training](file:///c:/Users/Admin/Documents/POC/Badminton/js/dashboard.js#L520-L534)

