## 3. ✅ Multi-Tenancy Isolation

**Yes, tenant data is isolated.** The isolation happens at **three layers**:

### Layer 1: User → Academy Binding
Each user document in `users/{email}` contains:
```json
{ "email": "user@example.com", "role": "TENANT_ADMIN", "academyId": "academy_xyz_123" }
```
At login, [checkUserAccess()](file:///c:/Users/Admin/Documents/POC/Badminton/js/shared.js#L445-L536) sets `currentUser.academyId` from the user document.

### Layer 2: Data Scoping (Every Query Uses academyId)
**Every single Firestore query** filters by `academyId`:

| Collection | Query Pattern |
|---|---|
| `bookings` | `where("academyId", "==", currentUser.academyId)` |
| `members` | `where("academyId", "==", currentUser.academyId)` |
| `courts` | `where("academyId", "==", currentUser.academyId)` |
| `academies` | Direct doc read: `doc(db, "academies", currentUser.academyId)` |

**Every write** stamps the document with `academyId: currentUser.academyId`:
```js
// Example from handleBookingSubmit:
{ booking_type: type, court_id: courtId, ..., academyId: currentUser.academyId }
```

### Layer 3: Firestore Security Rules (Server-Side Enforcement)
The [firestore.rules](file:///c:/Users/Admin/Documents/POC/Badminton/firestore.rules) enforce isolation at the database level:

```
function hasAcademyAccess(targetAcademyId) {
  return isAuthenticated() && (
    (isGuest() && targetAcademyId == 'demo_' + request.auth.uid) ||
    (!isGuest() && getUserData().academyId == targetAcademyId)
  );
}
```

Every collection rule uses this function:
```
match /bookings/{bookingId} {
  allow read:   if hasAcademyAccess(resource.data.get('academyId', ''));
  allow create: if hasAcademyAccess(request.resource.data.get('academyId', ''));
  allow update, delete: if hasAcademyAccess(resource.data.get('academyId', ''));
}
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This means even if someone tries to bypass the UI and directly query Firestore, **they can only read/write documents that belong to their own academy**. Tenant A cannot see Tenant B's bookings, members, or settings.

### Isolation Diagram:

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph "Tenant A (academy_abc)"
        A1["Settings/Programs"]
        A2["Bookings"]
        A3["Members"]
        A4["Courts"]
    end
    subgraph "Tenant B (academy_xyz)"
        B1["Settings/Programs"]
        B2["Bookings"]
        B3["Members"]
        B4["Courts"]
    end
    C["Firestore Security Rules"] -->|"academyId == user.academyId"| A1
    C -->|"academyId == user.academyId"| B1
    A1 -.->|"❌ Cannot access"| B2
    B1 -.->|"❌ Cannot access"| A2
```

